nswer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339910" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "Cx"] ["math" "C{x}^{2}"] ["math" "x"] ["math" "{x}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339910" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339910" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339910" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$"] ["text" "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339910" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $B$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+4y=3{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-4x},$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-x}$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-x}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an inhomogeneous differential equation, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}_{c}(x)$ is the complementary solution (the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous equation), and\n\n- ${y}_{p}(x)$ is a particular solution of the original inhomogeneous equation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check which of the two given functions is a particular solution of our inhomogeneous equation:\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({e}^{-x})^{′}=-{e}^{-x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(-{e}^{-x})^{′}={e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n({e}^{-x})+5(-{e}^{-x})+4({e}^{-x})=3{e}^{-x}.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-x}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =(x{e}^{-x})^{′}={e}^{-x}-x{e}^{-x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =({e}^{-x}-x{e}^{-x})^{′}=-2{e}^{-x}+x{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(-2{e}^{-x}+x{e}^{-x})+5({e}^{-x}-x{e}^{-x})+4(x{e}^{-x})=3{e}^{-x}.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-x}$ $\\text{is}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-4x}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-4x}+x{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a92ae8c3e61d85407dc3ab5f525e8bb61ae804a9a300402e981405d09c8211b6"} {"question" "q-339876" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339876" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "is"] ["text" "isn't"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063363/state.json" "file_sha256" "5394be542298dab6097c7663ece3dabbb9fc1a3e49ed07169af34705f8f48a67"} {"question" "q-339876" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "a